Title: SIGNAL LOSS
Author: Jordan Ellis
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - COMMAND DECK - DAY

DR. KARA VENN, 40s, monitors a wall of telemetry. A GOLD DATA CHIP rests beside her keyboard. The deep-space array pings — steady, then stutters.
KARA
Relay Seven, confirm packet integrity.
Static washes the speakers. One line of text resolves on screen: ORIGIN UNKNOWN.

INT. LUNAR MISSION CONTROL - DAY

CAPTAIN NOLAN REED, 50s, studies a holographic star map. LT. MARTINEZ enters with a printout.
MARTINEZ
Venn flagged an unregistered burst from the Kuiper corridor.
NOLAN
Tell her to hold the raw feed. If that signal's what I think, it's meant for me.

INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - SERVER BAY - NIGHT

Kara isolates the corrupted stream. She swaps the silver data chip into a portable reader. Decrypted fragments scroll — coordinates, a vessel ID.
KARA
Hull registry... that's been dark for twelve years.

EXT. LUNAR TRANSIT DOCK - NIGHT

Nolan crosses the gantry carrying a BLACK CASE. Dock workers salute as he boards a shuttle marked AURORA SIX.
NOLAN
Prep Aurora for an unscheduled outbound. Minimal crew.

INT. ORBITAL RELAY STATION - COMMAND DECK - DAY

Kara replays the signal. A grainy image resolves — a damaged hull, a flashing beacon. She reaches for her comm.
KARA
Nolan, the source is real. And it's asking for you by name.

FADE OUT.


THE END
